<pdd-reason>The sticky right-hand panel holding the app everyone is voting on. It is the payoff of the whole product: the thing the community asked for, running, one refresh away.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"SandboxPanel","signature":"function SandboxPanel(props: SandboxPanelProps): JSX.Element","returns":"the sticky preview aside"},
  {"name":"SandboxPanelProps","signature":"type SandboxPanelProps = { url: string | null; pulse?: boolean; onRefreshed?: () => void }","returns":"the component contract"}
]}}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>prompts/frontend/api_client_typescript.prompt</pdd-dependency>

Implement `frontend/src/components/sandbox_panel.tsx`. The shell passes `api_client.sandboxUrl`
straight through as `url`.

<responsibility>
Embed the live target app, and let a visitor pick up a new build without reloading the forum.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
This module DOES NOT resolve or validate the preview URL — `api_client` owns configuration and the host allowlist, and a `null` here means it already said no.
This module DOES NOT read `import.meta.env`.
This module DOES NOT compile, deploy, or know what changed in the build it is showing.
This module DOES NOT import `styles.css`; the shell imports it once for the whole app.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
**Sandbox** — the deployed target app (`streaks-demo`), hosted externally and embedded here. The local `TARGET_PROMPT_DIR` is the sprint service's compile target and has nothing to do with what the forum displays.
**Cold-start skeleton** — the placeholder shown until the frame reports `load`. The host sleeps free instances, so a first paint can take several seconds and an empty white box reads as the app being broken.
</vocabulary>

<capabilities>
- MAY hold the cache-busting nonce and the loaded flag.
- MUST NOT call `fetch`, `api_client`, or Supabase.
- MUST NOT add a hex value, font, radius, or animation — compose only `sandbox`, `sandbox-head`, `sandbox-sub`, `sandbox-frame-wrap`, `sandbox-skeleton`, `sandbox-newtab`, `sandbox-unavailable`, `refresh-btn`, `is-pulsing`.
</capabilities>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Render an `<aside class="sandbox">` containing `sandbox-head` (an `<h2>` reading `Sandbox` and a `sandbox-sub` reading `the app you're all building`), the framed embed, the refresh control, and the new-tab link, in that order.
R2 (MUST): Render the iframe inside `sandbox-frame-wrap` with a title naming it as the live preview, and set **no inline `style`** on it. The stylesheet sizes `.sandbox-frame-wrap iframe`; an inline `height: 100%` resolves against an auto-height parent and collapses the embed, silently overriding it. This has already happened once.
R3 (MUST): Give the iframe a restrictive `sandbox` attribute permitting scripts and same-origin for its own document only, and MUST NOT grant `allow-top-navigation`, `allow-popups`, or `allow-modals`. The embedded app is regenerated by an AI from community pitches; the forum should not hand it the ability to navigate away from, or overlay, the page hosting it.
R4 (MUST): Show the `sandbox-skeleton` reading `🔥 Warming up the sandbox…` until the frame fires `load`, and clear it after an 8-second timeout regardless. A blocked or sleeping host must degrade to a visible frame rather than spinning forever.
R5 (MUST): Reload the embed on the refresh control by bumping a nonce used both as the iframe `key` and as a `?v=` query parameter. The key remounts the element and the query defeats a cached build; either alone leaves a stale preview on screen some of the time.
R6 (MUST): Reset the skeleton on refresh, so the second load is as legible as the first.
R7 (MUST): Label the refresh control `↻ Refresh Preview`, and when `pulse` is set switch it to `✨ Refresh Preview — new build ready!` with `is-pulsing`. That glow is how a visitor learns their vote turned into a deploy.
R8 (MUST): Call `onRefreshed` when the control is pressed, so the shell can clear the pulse it raised.
R9 (MUST): Render `sandbox-unavailable` with an explanation — never a blank frame, a broken embed, or nothing — when `url` is `null`. Null means the URL was unset or failed the host allowlist, and a silently empty box reads as the app being down.
R10 (MUST): Render the `sandbox-newtab` link to the unmodified URL, with `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener noreferrer"`, and only when a URL exists. The embed is small and some visitors will want the real thing.
</contract_rules>

<pdd>
The panel is `position: sticky` in the stylesheet and becomes static below 960px — that is layout,
not this component's business, and it must not be reimplemented inline.

There is no `postMessage` channel to the embedded app and there should not be one: the target app
is regenerated from community pitches, so anything the forum listened for would be an interface an
AI could accidentally rewrite.
</pdd>

